# Orchestration artifacts (one file per lead-agent run) are local-only by
# default. They contain context-specific specialist outputs and intermediate
# data. Track them if your team requires the audit trail in version control.
#
# IMPORTANT — additive patterns only, never negations (`!pattern`).
# A .gitignore deeper in the tree outranks .git/info/exclude, so a negation
# here silently RE-INCLUDES the file and defeats a trial-mode install. This
# file previously used `*` plus `!.gitignore` / `!index.json`, which is exactly
# why those two showed up in `git status` after `--mode=trial`.
# Enforced by unit-gitignore-hygiene.sh.
*.specialist-outputs.json
